& [Fold1Identity] distinguishes four state categories
  + process state is one definition's instruction cursor local variables lifecycle and budget
  + serialized continuation is one yielded or waiting process state
  + coordination checkpoint is the complete deterministic scheduler frontier for all processes messages traces returns session and wake conditions
  + model context or hidden state is outside all three forms

& [Fold2Form] makes reentry complete and strict
  + checkpoint carries a profile exact input-lineage identities and digests slice index predecessor checkpoint digest all runtime products logical clock and checkpoint digest
  + no native host stack pointer thread handle closure ambient cache or process-global state is serialized
  + checkpoint JSON and optional schema reject unknown fields

& [Fold3Transition] separates start advance pause and finish
  + BEGIN validates existing invocation coordination and admission contracts then creates the same genesis runtime as uninterrupted coordination
  + ADVANCE requires a positive maximum step count and drives no more than that many process or scheduler steps
  + PAUSED returns one successor checkpoint while terminal returned faulted or budget-refused states return one existing CoordinationOutcome
  + global invocation budgets terminate rather than being disguised as a caller slice pause

& [Fold4Integrity] rejects forged trajectories
  + checkpoint digest is recomputed over every field except itself
  + request session catalogue procedure IR and admission inputs are rehashed or compared exactly on every advance
  + process state identities continuation digests map keys references frontiers lifecycle and sequence shapes are checked before execution
  + stale changed corrupt cross-invocation or zero-quota calls return no successor

& [Fold5Compatibility] preserves the original coordinator
  + coordinate_catalogued_procedure remains public with the same signature result and typed invalid-input behavior
  + it delegates genesis and driving to the same stepper with no artificial slice ceiling
  + terminal outcomes are byte-equal under uninterrupted one-step and multi-step chunk schedules for the same exact inputs

& [Fold6Proof] uses finite adversarial fixtures
  + BEGIN equals the original genesis state
  + repeated equal advance is byte-equal
  + quota one pauses and later resumes to the existing fifteen-step two-process terminal result
  + quota partitions one two four and large produce one exact terminal outcome
  + tampered digest altered request session procedure and state identity refuse before advancement
  + global step exhaustion remains BudgetRefused and existing coordination tests remain unchanged

& [Fold7Boundary] keeps P0 small
  + logical call frames subroutine call return recursion parsing IDE UI MCP exposure ledger storage persistence provider invocation and external effects are deferred
  + checkpoint hashing detects and binds content but does not authenticate its producer
  + a later host may pass checkpoint summaries between LLM passes but this runtime performs no inference

& [PrunedAlternatives] prevents parallel runtimes
  - do not create a second attention-specific instruction interpreter
  - do not store native stacks or Rust futures as continuation authority
  - do not make the new attention ledger implicitly accept CPPE checkpoints
  - do not represent caller slice exhaustion as an invocation fault

& [SelectedFlow] is validate exact inputs -> initialize or validate checkpoint -> drive bounded deterministic steps -> pause with digest-bound successor or finish with existing outcome
